Z||000013||EdsB52||07-17-2001||12:18 PM||||I have an 83 Chevy 3/4 pu that has 190,000 on it and is my savior. I have had probably 20 vehicles since I bought it in 1989 with 105,000 miles on it and it is always sitting there willing to take me to the part store or the machine shop to repair other vehicles. I think it was made in Canada. I was a japper then, but now only buy American, of course I never buy a new car. I like GM even though their politics suck in regard to what vehicles get developed, continued, or cut (Fiero, Camaro, etc). Jap stuff doesn't put out enough HP unless you spend gobs of money. Ford's suck in my opinion due to their non-interchangeability. Mopar stuff looks cool, but I don't know about their drivetrains.<P>A sample size of one or two isn't enough to reasonably evaluate anything, give it a chance.||||reg||1
Z||000014||firstfiero||07-17-2001||01:03 PM||||     One car!! Do any of you read long term testing? I've never read a good report on a gm....dodge and jeep usually get the lowest rating in every catagory!! And yes I know who made the engine in my storm. But let me point out another issue...body integrity. I had a 1980 bmw 528i befor my fiero. 220 thousand miles Not only could I still screech the tires in 3 gears but there were little to know rattles and noises from the body and interior. My geo storm with 20 grand on the odom. sounded like a rattle trap! junk....<P>------------------<BR><BR>   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/firstfiero.gif"> ||||reg||1
Z||000015||Slammed Fiero||07-17-2001||01:07 PM||||My brother has a pathfinder..loves it. We drove all the american competition and there was NO comparison. The pathfinder was far superior in every respect. Incl a 250hp 5spd to boot. <P>I have lost a lot of faith GM as an manufacturer. I Love the new ford explorer sport trac , Lincoln LS (DEW98 platform) , Toyota SUV's , Honda S2000 technology although it's powerband does nto appeal to me, Porsche , Audi.<P>No one does it better than the Germans for Cars. IF you disagree , you haven't driven one.<P>JM ||||reg||1
Z||000016||GOLDSE||07-17-2001||01:50 PM||||I think it's what you make of it.  I have a 69 Chevy Bel Air that suits me just fine.  Other than a little wear on the driver's seat and some surface rust on the exterior, great car.  Only replaced the water pump and it has 132,000 original miles.  <P>Wife has a 97 Cavalier that I'd like to get rid of.  Have had a 78 Honda Accord that was four different colors but ran like a champ.  That car never failed to take me anywhere and everywhere I wanted to go.  <P>It's all in the maintainance.  However, I do agree that yours could be the exception.  Just a bad apple. (lemon)||||reg||1
Z||000017||Black88GT||07-17-2001||04:12 PM||||OK I understand your frustrations but to generalize millions of cars based on one or two occurances is just ridiculous. <P>This topic comes up every once in a while (american vs. imports) or finds its way into other threads.  We can all post experiences until out fingers fall off, but it doesn't prove anything.  I can think of 3 experiences my family has had with Honda's that would make an ignorant person say "Honda's are junk".  But we all know they are not, we just had some problems with them (new and used).<P>My boss is a millionaire, and you know what he has for a daily driver?  A Bonneville.  He had a 93 or 94 that lasted like 190k miles, still ran but needed an exhaust I think, he traded it in for a new one.  Knowing how much money he has I asked why he didn't buy a BMW or Audi.  He told me that its cheaper overall to own and maintain his car then it would be for a new BMW.  He knows many people with them and the repairs are insanely expensive compared to the Bonneville.  This guy does his homework before just buying something, so he calculated initial price plus maintenance over a 7 year period his sister owned a BMW 4 door sedan (not sure exactly which model, it was a 3 series though) compared to the 7 year period he had his older Bonneville.  I think it was cheaper by about $17,000, don't have exact numbers but you get the point. <P>I think it should be noted also that VW's don't have such a great reliability record either.  Early/Mid-90s Jetta's had a fair share of problems.  Yet my Uncle had a 80s diesel Jetta that has a gazillion miles and still keeps going (see, there's another example for you).<P>While I agree German engineering is superior, there is something to be said for American engineers also.  I know I brought this up before but the Corvette just romped 3 German sports cars in a comparison.  <P>For me, it depends on what type of car in what price range you are looking for, you can't really say Japs make better cars period, there is more to it then that.  For example, Japanese sedans have no torque and look too plain for me.  I would much rather have a Grand Prix over a Camry or an Altima.  However, I love the Maxima SE and would much rather have that over a Bonneville SSEi.  Yet I would rather have the base model Bonneville over the base model Maxima (confusing aint it).  American car companies really don't impress me with 4 cyl. motors, so when my mom was looking in the sub $17k range for a new car, I told her to get a Sentra.   Cavaliers/Escorts/Neons don't bring up reliability in my mind when I think about them.  She ended up getting a fully loaded SE for around 16,500 with a 100k mile warranty.  I have much more faith in that then in a Neon.  <P>BTW, how are those Canadian cars doing? Oh yeah thats right they don't make any.... ||||reg||1
Z||000018||Slammed Fiero||07-17-2001||04:27 PM||||ahh..<P>FYI ..GM is originally Mclaughlin ..a Candian Company.. (I learned this my first day working at GM)<P>The Camaro is made in QUEBEC..Last I checked they were part of Canada...<P>GM trucks I believe are made in Canada...and the CK truck Division sponsored the corvette from 73 when it started loosing money to 97 when it actually managed to stay on it's own 2 feet without the help of the truck division.<BR>I don't remember off hand what other cars are made here...but you made a good try for a grossly mis informed individual.<P>GM was BORN Canadian, read a history book <P>JM <p>[This message has been edited by Slammed Fiero (edited 07-17-2001).]||||reg||1
