Z||000027||AusFiero||07-19-2001||10:27 AM||||Having owned many makes from all over the world I will agree that Germans do make fine cars. I am not including Volkswagon, personally I think they are the pits. <P>My favourite car for quality versus price though would be products made by Subaru. Do they send good Subarus to America or just base model runabouts? I have had a couple and my bro-inlaw has a fleet of the things in his business. They are well made, very reliable and take a caning when you need to give em one. <P>Ok mine was a Subaru WRX turbo 4X4 which was built for the track more than the road, but all the others I have driven have been really tight cars with doors that click closed after 200,000 KMS etc. I know GM's here or in the USA aren't built that good in comparison.  <P>------------------<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.jadeweb.com.au/fiero/ausfiero1.gif"> <BR><A HREF="http://www.jadeweb.com.au/fiero" TARGET=_blank>My Fiero</A> | <A HREF="http://www.auto-alley.com" TARGET=_blank>Fiero Accessories</A>||202.139.20.3||reg||1
